# World 2's strait destroyer (SPEC 11, "World 2, slice 2", slice E). Ctrl+L, W, 6 starts mission 6, Typhoon Strait; skill 1 is pinned after the
# world has loaded (the longest tells, no wind and no early jets: the same fight every time), ghost on (a hit is shown and shrugged off).
# Ctrl+L, D puts the chopper low over the water 94 px east of the aft turret: the turret turns, its barrel rises and flashes (a tell of 28
# frames on skill 1), then the shell. A climb brings the AA guns in (flak: the barrel up, a ranging puff, the burst); then low again, the cannon
# takes the aft turret (6 hits), a move west the forward one: both dead and the hull lists, "DEST DWN" in the HUD, 400 points.
# The unit tests (testW2Destroyer*, testW2Turret*, testW2Aa*) hold the rules.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x06
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 1500
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x01
wait 30
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x24
wait 30
screenshot card
press fire 2
wait 60
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x22
wait 10
screenshot approach
wait-serial "AGK destroyer tell" 400
wait 14
screenshot tell
wait-serial "AGK destroyer fire" 100
wait 3
screenshot shot
# climb into the guns' reach: the flak
press up 25
wait-serial "AGK flak tell" 400
wait 10
screenshot flaktell
wait-serial "AGK flak burst" 100
wait 3
screenshot burst
# low again, and the cannon: the aft turret
press down 40
wait 20
press fire 90
wait-serial "AGK turret down=1" 200
wait 20
screenshot smoking
# the forward turret: west, then the cannon
press left 10
wait 30
press fire 90
wait-serial "AGK turret down=2" 300
wait-serial "AGK destroyer down" 20
wait 25
screenshot listing
wait 100
expect-serial "AGK destroyer tell[\s\S]*AGK destroyer fire[\s\S]*AGK flak tell[\s\S]*AGK flak burst[\s\S]*AGK turret down=1[\s\S]*AGK turret down=2[\s\S]*AGK destroyer down"
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 98
expect-min-chip-free 96
